{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 3.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the $3.00 CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) gantry line on fare breakdown EV-FARE-00310 has no counterpart anywhere in GPS trace EV-GPS-00310 — the nearest fix is 5,551 m away, far outside the 250 m crossing radius — so the line is refunded in full as a standalone correction and this billing-integrity finding is recorded."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you: the outcome is a partial refund of SGD 3.00 to the rider. Here is how each part of the claim is decided.\n\n1. The CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) ERP line — the rider is right. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00310) bills $3.00 for that gantry, but the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00310) — 157 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, maximum gap 0 seconds — never comes within 5,551 m of it, over twenty times the 250 m radius POL-RD-09(4) uses to treat a fix as a crossing. The fare breakdown itself flags the line on_optimal_route false. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure and is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not any deviation exists. This refund is unaffected by cause or fault: the driver's point that 'ERP is automatic from the IU, I cannot control it' is no answer to a line the vehicle never triggered.\n\n2. The ECP (Fort Rd towards City) ERP line — the driver is right. The $2.00 charge is matched at 0 m by fix index 54 at 08:29:25, well inside the 250 m radius, and it is flagged on_optimal_route true; the platform's booked optimal route is 'ECP then Nicoll Hwy' with an optimal-route ERP of $2.00 (trip record EV-TRIP-00310). It is a properly chargeable on-route pass-through and it stands. The rider's premise that the ECP gantry is $2.00 is in fact met by the ledger.\n\n3. The route-deviation head of claim ('he went a longer way than needed') — not established. The trace governs under POL-RD-01: 13.7 km against a booked optimal of 13.0 km, an excess of 0.70 km, or 5.38%. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH an excess greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%; neither test passes, so no deviation exists. Both advocates reached this result and I agree. Consequently POL-RD-02 does not run, and the recomputation the fare ledger carries ($19.67 recomputed fare, $5.49 refund against $25.16 charged) presupposes an established deviation and is not payable. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 opens no alternative route. The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is met on identification (trip_id TRP-00310 matches across trip record, trace and fare breakdown) but not on the threshold limb, so no burden shifts to the driver.\n\n4. Escalation — none. The trip identifiers match, the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c), and the only charge line without a trace counterpart is the CTE line, which is refunded under POL-RD-09(4) and is expressly carved out of POL-RD-10(8). The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00310-01 (status MISSING, weight 0.0) is not relied on by either party as an external traffic cause, so POL-RD-13 and POL-RD-10(5) are not engaged.\n\n5. Conduct — no referral. No MATERIAL deviation exists on this trip (5.38% / 0.70 km), and the driver's trailing-90-day counter is 0 deviation flags across 260 completed trips (driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d, EV-DPROF-00310), so no repeat pattern is established under POL-RD-06 and no POL-RD-06(c) review fires. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used as a ground.\n\nConfidence: the ruling rests on the GPS trace (weight 1.0) and the fare breakdown (weight 1.0), both at full weight; the missing advisory carries no deciding fact and does not lower the cap. Confidence 0.90, above the 0.70 floor. The refund of SGD 3.00 does not exceed the SGD 8.00 execution threshold and executes automatically. The single billing-integrity finding above is recorded as a POL-RD-09(4) referral."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
