      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity: fare_breakdown line \"CTE (Braddell Rd towards City)\" for SGD 3.00 on TRP-00310 has no gps_trace fix within the 250 m match radius (nearest fix 5,551 m); refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver, this is decided on the trip's own records.\n\nROUTE COMPLAINT — not upheld. The platform's booked optimal was 13.0 km; the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00310) measures 13.7 km, an excess of 0.70 km (5.38%). POL-RD-01 requires BOTH an excess greater than 0.8 km AND greater than 20% before a deviation is established, and neither is met, so no deviation exists and no distance-or-time refund arises. The trace is unimpaired — 157 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s — so POL-RD-07 does not engage and nothing needed corroborating. The POL-RD-02 recomputation the fare ledger carries (charged_total 25.16; recomputed_fare 19.67; refund 5.50) presupposes an established deviation and is NOT payable. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-11 opens no alternative route either.\n\nERP COMPLAINT — upheld in part. The receipt carries ERP of 5.00: ECP (Fort Rd towards City) 2.00, which the trace passes at 0 m and which is flagged on-route, and CTE (Braddell Rd towards City) 3.00, which the trace never comes within 5,551 m of. Under POL-RD-09(4) a gantry line the gps_trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction whether or not a deviation exists. Refund: SGD 3.00. Your premise that the ECP gantry is $2.00 was right — the ledger charges exactly 2.00 there — and the overcharge is the 3.00 CTE line, not the whole 5.00.\n\nDriver: your statement that 'ERP is automatic from the IU, I cannot control it' does not answer POL-RD-09(4); the correction is fault-independent, and the vehicle did not cross the Braddell gantry. Your account that the route was 'normal ECP' is borne out by the trace and by the booked optimal route ('ECP then Nicoll Hwy'), and no adverse routing finding is made against you. No repeat-deviation pattern arises under POL-RD-06 (deviation_flags_90d 0 against 260 completed trips); the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used.\n\nThe missing traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00310-01, status MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) is noted: it is a citable absence, but no party asserted an external traffic cause, so it affects nothing here.\n\nThe 3.00 correction exceeds the 0.50 de minimis. The monetary effect (3.00) is below the 8.00 execution threshold, so it executes automatically. The deciding fact is carried by artifacts at weight 1.0, so confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor and no escalation is required. A billing-integrity referral is recorded under POL-RD-09(4)."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
